  "validation_limits": [
    "Fifteen complete native translation units compile with all 24 composed patches. Baseline objects use the original public source, not the preceding capture parent.",
    "Emitted submitter increments queue ownership under the mutex before publication. Release decrements under the mutex, unlocks, and inserts into the free queue only when the count reaches zero.",
    "Emitted reset marks the sticky bit before signaling -1 under the mutex. Completion skips result overwrite when that bit is set, clears the matching current pointer, signals, unlocks, and drops the queue/worker reference. Waiter copies the result under the same mutex.",
    "Worker EXIT comparison uses the cached opcode after completion. Selected function-control wrapper logs its saved parameters after submission returns. Native hardware/software reset calls remain present.",
    "Native compiler flags include -w; empty diagnostics do not establish warning-clean code.",
    "Thirteen directed pthread fixture cases exercise actual selected WMT functions with injected queues/core execution. They do not execute the kernel completion implementation or real reset machinery.",
    "No full kernel link, reset/resource isolation, repair of other diagnostic clients post-submit accesses, library reinitialization support, whole-request capture attribution, timing budget, boot candidate or device execution."
  ]
}
